From 9f18048a2052072166ccc3b0ffef364e72bb4d11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AviBackToBlack <AviBackToBlack@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 11:11:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: native CUDA port for v0.27.1 on SM120

Establish the first fully accepted native Windows milestone on RTX 5090 / Blackwell SM120.

Includes Windows build/runtime support for the core vLLM extensions plus FlashAttention 2, FlashKDA, QuTLASS and DeepGEMM plumbing; CUDA 13 / PyTorch cu130 dependency metadata; Windows filesystem, IPC, asyncio, signal/process cleanup and optional-dependency compatibility fixes.

Validated from a pristine wheel install with 9 native extensions, default-performance offline generation, Inductor/AOT/CUDAGraphs, and OpenAI-compatible /v1/models and /v1/completions HTTP generation.

DeepGEMM binary/JIT plumbing is present, but upstream DeepGEMM 2.6.1 still has no SM120 runtime kernel dispatch. FA3 is intentionally absent because upstream FA3 does not support SM120.
